WEBVTT

00:01.600 --> 00:04.700
Ikusen no namida o koe

00:04.700 --> 00:08.270
Omoi wa kouya o yuku

00:08.270 --> 00:16.180
Itsuka kizu wa ieru kara saa trust myself

00:21.350 --> 00:27.990
Yaketsuku hizashi no moto kimi wa nani omou?

00:27.990 --> 00:33.900
Urei no hitomi wa ima nani o utsusu?

00:33.900 --> 00:42.840
Mayowazu ni irareru no nara
step by step tayasui darou

00:42.840 --> 00:47.540
Kaze no you ni

00:47.540 --> 00:50.650
Ikusen no namida o koe

00:50.650 --> 00:54.150
Akatsuki no kouya o yuku

00:54.150 --> 01:00.690
Itsuka kizu wa ieru kara saa trust myself

01:00.690 --> 01:07.430
Don't be afraid kawaru koto wa
osoreru koto ja nai

01:07.430 --> 01:13.570
Kimi ga kimi de aru naraba will be with you

01:13.570 --> 01:20.240
Odayaka na hi o yume-mite

01:20.240 --> 01:27.550
Michi-naki tabiji wa tsuzuku

01:54.080 --> 01:55.570
Oops!

01:59.080 --> 02:01.240
That Miguel...

02:12.260 --> 02:14.760
You screwed up again, Miguel.

02:14.760 --> 02:19.000
It's more fun for the audience
when these incidents happen, right?

02:19.000 --> 02:21.490
You're a smoother talker
than you are a guitar player!

02:25.340 --> 02:26.770
So she's a first-rate pro?

02:26.770 --> 02:29.080
She's damn lucky, that's for sure.

02:29.080 --> 02:31.750
Well, that's probably all it is.

02:31.750 --> 02:33.740
Thank you for waiting.

02:37.620 --> 02:40.460
- Hey.
- Y-Yes, sir?

02:40.460 --> 02:43.630
If you see them, give us a call.

02:43.630 --> 02:46.930
We're staying at the hotel on the corner.

02:46.930 --> 02:51.330
That's a bounty. The one
in the photo to the right.

02:51.330 --> 02:54.270
And the one on the left is
the little bounty hunter girl.

02:54.270 --> 02:58.770
If we succeed in taking them
down, we'll give you a cut.

02:58.770 --> 03:00.760
Thank you very much.

03:04.150 --> 03:07.270
A little girl?

03:11.890 --> 03:14.950
That's Nadie.

03:20.160 --> 03:21.900
"'Oh, Miguel...

03:21.900 --> 03:27.340
I've been in love with you since
the day I first laid eyes on you.'

03:27.340 --> 03:29.070
'Me, too, Nadia.

03:29.070 --> 03:32.910
I can't imagine life without you.'

03:32.910 --> 03:40.370
The incandescent flames of love
blazed in Miguel and Nadia's hearts."

03:42.720 --> 03:47.090
Nadie, about how hot are the flames of love?

03:47.090 --> 03:50.180
- Beats me.
- You don't know?

03:51.990 --> 03:54.000
That stuff is pure fiction.

03:54.000 --> 03:56.000
When you get down to it, love is just a game.

03:56.000 --> 03:59.900
It's fool or be fooled. That's all that
happens between men and women.

04:02.700 --> 04:05.110
Do you... hate men?

04:05.110 --> 04:06.940
No, no.

04:09.080 --> 04:10.910
No, no!

04:12.380 --> 04:15.120
Sure, I'm the one who suggested
that you buy a book or something,

04:15.120 --> 04:18.190
because our time on the bus
would get boring, but...

04:18.190 --> 04:21.220
You didn't have to pick such a trashy novel.

04:21.220 --> 04:23.360
The names were similar.

04:23.360 --> 04:25.860
That's actually the part that
got on my nerves the most.

04:25.860 --> 04:27.900
Especially the guy's name...

04:27.900 --> 04:29.560
Miguel?

04:31.070 --> 04:34.300
Hey, Nadie! It's you!

04:34.300 --> 04:36.900
D-Don't tell me...

04:38.210 --> 04:41.940
I knew it was you, Nadie! Long time no see!

04:41.940 --> 04:43.710
I've missed you!

04:49.620 --> 04:54.320
The incandescent flames of love blazed...

04:55.760 --> 04:58.390
Your punches are the same as ever.

04:58.390 --> 05:01.920
And your face seems as thick-skinned as ever.

05:06.430 --> 05:09.070
But talk about a real coincidence.

05:09.070 --> 05:12.070
I never imagined we'd be
reunited in a town like this.

05:12.070 --> 05:13.570
I sense destiny at work.

05:13.570 --> 05:16.240
- I don't.
- Really?

05:16.240 --> 05:19.150
Then, could the one I'm destined for...

05:19.150 --> 05:21.480
...be this young lady over here?

05:23.250 --> 05:25.290
Don't take him seriously, Ellis.

05:25.290 --> 05:27.090
I told you just earlier, remember?

05:27.090 --> 05:29.590
You can't trust men.

05:29.590 --> 05:33.090
You're awful, Nadie. Saying stuff like that...

05:33.090 --> 05:35.460
Could it be that you're
still mad about that thing?

05:35.460 --> 05:37.530
Beats me. What are you talking about?

05:37.530 --> 05:42.600
Since you seem to have
forgotten, I'll tell the story.

05:42.600 --> 05:44.270
Our relationship was...

05:44.270 --> 05:48.000
Miguel, are you looking to get hit again?

05:57.320 --> 05:59.520
How long are you going
to sit there eating, Nadie?

05:59.520 --> 06:01.820
It's almost check-in time.

06:01.820 --> 06:03.730
But I...

06:03.730 --> 06:08.820
You were hired out of charity, so you
need to pull your weight around here!

06:11.500 --> 06:14.300
Ms. Luiz, the manager's looking for you.

06:14.300 --> 06:16.330
Oh, what could he want?

06:20.640 --> 06:23.840
The manager's actually out
on some minor business.

06:26.250 --> 06:30.050
The others probably forced their
chores on you anyway, right?

06:30.050 --> 06:31.990
Take your time eating.

06:31.990 --> 06:34.550
Thank you, Miguel.

06:54.180 --> 07:01.020
You really do need a good instrument
to become a first-rate mariachi.

07:01.020 --> 07:03.540
Playing a cheap instrument
like this, I'll never...

07:07.190 --> 07:12.250
If only I had a little more money,
I could at least buy a better one...

07:17.030 --> 07:20.540
At this rate, I might end up getting fired...

07:20.540 --> 07:22.270
Here.

07:22.270 --> 07:24.210
Will this be enough?

07:24.210 --> 07:25.570
That's your pay, isn't it?

07:25.570 --> 07:26.810
I couldn't take that...

07:26.810 --> 07:30.480
It's okay. I have a little
saved up and besides...

07:30.480 --> 07:33.210
I have nothing to spend it on anyway.

07:33.210 --> 07:36.420
Let me hear you put on a
great performance, Miguel.

07:36.420 --> 07:37.910
Nadie!

07:45.460 --> 07:48.120
I'll be sure to put it to good use.

07:52.130 --> 07:53.970
It looks fabulous on you!

07:53.970 --> 07:56.670
It's like it makes your
beauty shine even brighter!

07:56.670 --> 07:59.410
Are you really sure I can have this, Miguel?

07:59.410 --> 08:02.580
I came into a bit of a windfall yesterday.

08:02.580 --> 08:06.070
So I thought I'd take my good
fortune and spend it on you.

08:13.590 --> 08:16.960
Nadie... Oh, right, you must be
on your way back from shopping.

08:16.960 --> 08:19.360
Do you have a little free time later?

08:19.360 --> 08:21.760
There's a lot that I want to talk to you about.

08:29.600 --> 08:31.330
To hell with men...

08:32.940 --> 08:36.840
I really feel bad about what I did that time.

08:36.840 --> 08:41.220
But I've had a change of heart since then.

08:41.220 --> 08:44.620
I've become a fine mariachi now.

08:44.620 --> 08:46.050
Thanks for the meal.

08:46.050 --> 08:48.220
Let me thank you for what you did back then.

08:48.220 --> 08:50.560
Naturally, I'll also pay you
back the money I owe you.

08:50.560 --> 08:52.660
Those tacos were plenty.

08:52.660 --> 08:54.200
Ellis, let's go.

08:54.200 --> 08:55.700
Yessir.

08:55.700 --> 09:00.300
I'll be waiting in front of the
big clock in the square tonight.

09:00.300 --> 09:02.290
I'll keep waiting for you.

09:30.700 --> 09:33.000
Man, I'm beat!

09:33.000 --> 09:35.230
Let's take a nap, Ellis.

09:38.440 --> 09:40.680
Aren't you going?

09:40.680 --> 09:42.010
I told you, didn't I?

09:42.010 --> 09:44.750
You can't trust men.

09:44.750 --> 09:46.610
Especially not him.

09:46.610 --> 09:51.250
He's become a fine mariachi?
It's bound to be a lie.

09:51.250 --> 09:53.890
Even if I were to head out there like a fool,

09:53.890 --> 09:58.730
I'd only end up getting bamboozled
out of more money anyway.

09:58.730 --> 10:01.920
I've had enough of being tricked by men.

10:53.610 --> 10:56.640
I know he has no plans to pay me back...

11:04.590 --> 11:08.320
To think you'd leave my
Ellis all by her lonesome...

11:20.170 --> 11:23.300
But it can't be helped, right?

11:29.180 --> 11:33.980
You lose sight of everything around
you when you fall in love, after all.

11:49.070 --> 11:52.560
I guess Nadie's smartened up a little.

11:56.510 --> 11:58.070
Miguel?

12:01.880 --> 12:04.080
I've been waiting for you, Nadie.

12:23.440 --> 12:26.440
My friend's waiting for me in our room.

12:26.440 --> 12:28.840
If you're worried,
why don't you give her a call?

12:28.840 --> 12:30.850
And tell her you're going
to be out late tonight.

12:30.850 --> 12:33.910
Quit fooling around and pay
me back what you owe me.

12:33.910 --> 12:37.020
Thanks to you, I was able
to become an honest man.

12:37.020 --> 12:40.420
I could spend the whole night thanking
you and it still wouldn't be enough.

12:42.360 --> 12:45.350
I thank the Lord for reuniting us.

12:51.030 --> 12:52.620
Cheers.

13:03.740 --> 13:05.910
Oh, man...

13:08.050 --> 13:10.990
Honestly! What are you thinking?!

13:10.990 --> 13:14.280
He's a good-for-nothing!
A good-for-nothing! A good-for-nothing!

13:16.720 --> 13:18.210
Huh?

13:22.160 --> 13:24.060
I wonder if he's gone to the bathroom...

13:34.340 --> 13:37.950
Say, would you happen to
know where my friend went?

13:37.950 --> 13:40.110
No.

13:40.110 --> 13:42.680
The man I was drinking with...
have you seen him?

13:42.680 --> 13:44.290
No idea...

13:44.290 --> 13:46.520
Does anyone know where my friend went?

13:46.520 --> 13:48.950
His name's Miguel and he's a mariachi.

13:51.590 --> 13:54.960
If it's your friend, he left by himself earlier.

13:54.960 --> 13:57.120
Trying to trick me again?!

13:58.770 --> 14:01.700
Would you happen to know which
establishment Miguel works at?

14:03.300 --> 14:07.440
Oh, Miguel's definitely one of our mariachis.

14:07.440 --> 14:09.110
Up until three days ago, that is.

14:09.110 --> 14:10.510
Three days ago?

14:10.510 --> 14:15.880
Meaning we were sick of putting up
with his crappy performances.

14:18.220 --> 14:21.790
I don't know what your relationship is with him,

14:21.790 --> 14:24.190
but I'll give you a word of advice.

14:24.190 --> 14:27.160
Don't trust that guy.

14:27.160 --> 14:29.230
He's nothing but a womanizer.

14:29.230 --> 14:32.500
I don't need you... to tell me that...

14:32.500 --> 14:35.540
I don't know where he is right now,

14:35.540 --> 14:37.640
but it sounded like he had something going on.

14:37.640 --> 14:42.140
He said something about an old
friend bringing a cash cow soon.

14:42.140 --> 14:45.080
An old friend?

14:45.080 --> 14:46.570
It can't be!

14:51.820 --> 14:53.150
Who's there?

14:53.150 --> 14:55.490
It's Miguel. We met this afternoon?

14:55.490 --> 14:57.830
Nadie's asking for you.

14:57.830 --> 14:59.220
Nadie...

15:00.530 --> 15:02.020
Yeah.

15:13.910 --> 15:15.540
We're getting off.

15:19.080 --> 15:20.570
Ellis!

15:26.220 --> 15:30.690
If it's your friend, she just
left earlier with a man.

15:30.690 --> 15:31.690
Where did they go?

15:31.690 --> 15:34.090
That, I wouldn't know...

15:35.530 --> 15:37.520
M-Ma'am...

15:39.230 --> 15:40.790
This...

16:02.160 --> 16:03.990
Where's Nadie?

16:05.290 --> 16:09.960
Yeah, she should be here soon.

16:09.960 --> 16:12.460
Hey there, you're late, Lourdes...

16:14.570 --> 16:16.940
H-Hey there, it's you guys...

16:16.940 --> 16:21.410
I thought we told you to let us
know right away if you found her.

16:21.410 --> 16:23.810
Of course, I hadn't forgotten.

16:23.810 --> 16:25.750
I had one little thing to take care of,

16:25.750 --> 16:28.680
but after that, I was planning on
bringing her to where you're staying.

16:28.680 --> 16:31.750
Oh, yeah, if you're willing
to give me my cut right away,

16:31.750 --> 16:33.790
I'd be fine with handing her
over to you here and now.

16:33.790 --> 16:37.020
I need money. How much will you give me?

16:41.930 --> 16:45.500
If you want, we could
give you our entire fortune!

16:45.500 --> 16:47.270
Really?

16:47.270 --> 16:49.930
Since we'd be getting it right back anyway.

16:53.440 --> 16:55.440
Wh-Why?

16:55.440 --> 16:58.180
You apparently have trouble
keeping your hands off the ladies.

16:58.180 --> 17:01.820
- What?
- The boss of a certain town
is quite angry with you.

17:01.820 --> 17:04.320
Saying you ruined his daughter!

17:04.320 --> 17:06.450
So, this is what happened.

17:06.450 --> 17:10.620
It got sent to every hotel
in the area just earlier.

17:10.620 --> 17:13.390
You've got quite a price on your head.

17:13.390 --> 17:15.560
We sure are lucky.

17:15.560 --> 17:18.630
We were waiting for our goose
and a golden egg came along with it.

17:18.630 --> 17:23.140
Th-That guy again?! I get
mistaken for him a lot! It's true!

17:23.140 --> 17:25.170
This is just a case of mistaken identity!

17:25.170 --> 17:27.640
I'm just a poor mariachi.

17:27.640 --> 17:31.010
I would never consider laying a hand
on the daughter of some big boss...

17:31.010 --> 17:34.980
"A glib-talking mariachi."
The description's a match.

17:34.980 --> 17:37.990
Like I said, the guy you
want is a mariachi, too.

17:37.990 --> 17:39.490
If you want, I could take you to him now...

17:39.490 --> 17:42.820
It also says to watch out
for your slippery talk.

17:42.820 --> 17:46.020
And that they'll take you dead or alive.

17:47.830 --> 17:51.760
I've got a great moneymaking scheme, so...

18:02.180 --> 18:06.750
He may be a worthless liar, but he's
still an old acquaintance of mine.

18:06.750 --> 18:08.850
Nadie!

18:08.850 --> 18:10.840
Ellis, where are you?

18:12.550 --> 18:16.020
- Here.
- Get inside, turn the
lights out, and don't move.

18:16.020 --> 18:17.510
Yessir.

18:21.860 --> 18:24.360
If you'll back off quietly, that's fine.

18:24.360 --> 18:28.360
But if you have no intention of
doing that, I'll give you a little time.

18:29.770 --> 18:32.970
If you have any last words, say them now.

18:34.780 --> 18:37.210
I hear there's a bunch of bounty hunters

18:37.210 --> 18:38.910
shooting at each other in a parking lot nearby!

18:38.910 --> 18:41.710
Whoa, talk about dangerous!

18:53.390 --> 18:55.730
Ellis, you alive?

18:56.900 --> 18:58.590
Alive.

18:59.770 --> 19:02.070
Miguel, it's over.

19:02.070 --> 19:05.110
I've got a lot of questions for you.

19:05.110 --> 19:06.940
Come on out.

19:09.140 --> 19:12.310
Miguel, the coast's clear already.

19:16.920 --> 19:18.580
Miguel?

19:20.350 --> 19:22.420
Miguel!

19:22.420 --> 19:25.760
Hang in there! Miguel! Miguel?!

19:25.760 --> 19:30.660
Why, Miguel?! You said you'd leave town with me!

19:37.640 --> 19:39.630
Let's go, Ellis.

19:44.610 --> 19:46.100
Ellis.

20:00.830 --> 20:02.960
Morning, Miss Hayward.

20:02.960 --> 20:05.630
Good morning, Mr. Rosenberg.

20:05.630 --> 20:08.870
Oh, yes, if I might have a word.

20:08.870 --> 20:11.870
I was going to speak with you about this later,

20:11.870 --> 20:15.640
but it seems documents are being
submitted rather late recently,

20:15.640 --> 20:18.050
so I wanted to ask you to be mindful of that.

20:18.050 --> 20:19.650
I understand.

20:19.650 --> 20:22.550
I will issue a stern warning to my subordinates.

20:22.550 --> 20:24.180
Bye now.

20:27.590 --> 20:30.020
Subordinates, is it?

20:40.700 --> 20:45.930
It seems I really will need
to issue a stern warning.

21:08.530 --> 21:11.060
It turned out just like I said, right?

21:11.060 --> 21:14.870
Men are a breed you just can't trust.

21:14.870 --> 21:18.930
So you must never carelessly
go anywhere with them.

21:20.140 --> 21:22.730
But you went with him.

21:26.050 --> 21:30.110
And that woman said she was
planning on going with him, too.

21:31.220 --> 21:32.890
You're right.

21:32.890 --> 21:35.490
I'm sure there were many other women

21:35.490 --> 21:37.560
who were deceived by him, too.

21:37.560 --> 21:41.220
- Was he a bad man?
- Yup, a bad guy.

21:43.400 --> 21:44.500
But you know,

21:44.500 --> 21:49.270
even when you know that,
sometimes, you just can't hate them.

21:49.270 --> 21:53.070
That's especially true between men and women...

21:55.110 --> 21:59.000
Why not?

22:00.950 --> 22:02.980
The incandescent flames of love...

22:02.980 --> 22:05.110
It's not like that!

22:13.690 --> 22:16.290
There's no reason for you to be crying!

22:19.000 --> 22:21.600
Why are you crying?!

22:21.600 --> 22:23.800
Why?

22:23.800 --> 22:25.810
Oh, honestly!

22:25.810 --> 22:27.800
Never mind, just don't cry!

22:30.510 --> 22:32.380
Yessir.

22:36.620 --> 22:40.350
Owaranai natsu no you ni

22:40.350 --> 22:43.890
Chiranai hana no you ni

22:43.890 --> 22:47.790
Dakishimeta sono ude o

22:47.790 --> 22:55.960
Zutto hanasanaide ite yo

23:02.210 --> 23:05.710
Sugari-tsuite-mitemo

23:05.710 --> 23:11.490
Mune wa mada chigau hakanasa de

23:11.490 --> 23:15.420
Toki no rizumu kazoeteru

23:15.420 --> 23:19.560
Akai hoshi no yoru

23:19.560 --> 23:23.560
Kiete-yuku nukumori

23:23.560 --> 23:27.500
Tsunagi-tometai no yo

23:27.500 --> 23:34.010
Hitomi tojita kimi o

23:34.010 --> 23:37.940
Akogare o kuri-kaeshi

23:37.940 --> 23:41.380
Doko e mo yukenaku-temo

23:41.380 --> 23:45.420
Setsunasa no tachidomaru

23:45.420 --> 23:51.790
Kono hito-toki ga futari no

23:51.790 --> 23:56.790
Subete yo
